					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-343775#post-2489948</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-343775/scp-931#post-2489948</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Mon, 11 Apr 2016 20:51:12 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>SunRat</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>2206367</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Not downvoting because of this, since I really like the article (even though, technically it should be an anomalous item not a full SCiP); but&#8230;</p> <p>A haiku is a nature poem. Period. The 5-7-5 structure is not necessary, and many haiku are in a 10-7, or 12-5 structure. All that matters is that there are only 17 syllables.</p> <p>A 17 syllable poem that is not a nature poem is properly termed a <em>senryu</em>. It uses the 17 syllable structure, but is not a nature poem (it's typically social commentary or satire).</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
